8-Queens :
8 x 8 = 64. Your DFS tree has 64 nodes in it and each node has maxIndex of 2 (0 or 1 where 1 indicates you have a queen at that spot)

That's it


Sudoku:
9 x 9 where same row, column and 3x3 block must have all the numbers from 1..9 only once

It is a 9 x 9 = 81 DFS tree where repetitions are allowed thus each node can have maxIndex of 9. So fill up your 81 DFS graph an trivially
cull early where possible and beyond that it is exactly the same problem as above

